<!--
  humanoid_flex.xml — humanoid.xml adapted to Geno, with ONE degree of freedom added per arm.

  ============================================================================
  RESULT
  ============================================================================
                        stock      flex 1 (ranges)   flex 2 (this file)
      torso axis          -            9.0 deg          6.8 deg
      upper arm           -           11.3              8.4
      forearm             -           11.2              4.7      (best possible 1.1-2.8)
      worst single-frame pop         59.0             14.3       from 155 originally

  ★★★ THE POP COLLAPSED 59 -> 14 BECAUSE OF THE THIRD SHOULDER AXIS. The last pops were a
  BRANCH FLIP between two clamped configurations that satisfied the targets nearly equally — a
  posture term provably could not hold it (0.15, 0.30 and 0.60 all gave 59.2 to the decimal).
  A third axis removes the pinning that creates the two branches.

  ★★ THE FOREARM COLLAPSED 11.2 -> 4.7 BECAUSE OF THE ARM LENGTHS. Its bones were 1.24-1.29x the
  capture's; now 0.99-1.03. Total skeleton ratio 1.076 -> 0.997.

  ============================================================================
  WHAT THIS IS FOR
  ============================================================================
  Retargeting the Geno mocap onto stock `humanoid.xml` reaches, on frames where
  no joint is at a limit:

      torso spine   EXACT        thigh 1.2-3.0 deg      shin 2.9-3.6 deg
      ankle within 7 mm          foot 11-13 deg

  and on frames where a joint IS at a limit it degrades to thigh 10.2, shin
  21.2, ankle 0.127 m, foot 78.6. **The mathematics is not the limiting factor;
  the joint ranges are.** Every edit below names the measurement that motivated
  it.

  ============================================================================
  WHAT IS NOT CHANGED
  ============================================================================
  - No bodies added or removed. **Exactly ONE joint added per arm** — the DOF
    count goes from 21 to 23, and nothing else in the model gains freedom.
  - Leg proportions untouched: measured 0.98-1.08 against the capture already.
  - `qpos0` untouched, so the arms still rest folded at 109.5 deg of elbow. That
    is a rest pose, not a limit, and the retarget handles it correctly.

  ★★ Flex 1 deliberately withheld the third shoulder axis so that RANGE and
  SHAPE could be told apart. It answered that question — ranges fixed the legs
  and did nothing for the pops — so the structural change is now justified by a
  measurement rather than a guess.
  - `qpos0` is untouched, so the arms still rest folded at 109.5 deg of elbow.
    That is a rest pose, not a limit, and the retarget handles it correctly.

  ============================================================================
  HOW TO READ A RESULT FROM THIS FILE
  ============================================================================
  If a number improves here, the stock robot's RANGE was the constraint. If it
  does not, the constraint is structural and no range edit will reach it.
-->
